WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.669
-We're hanging out with
Barbra Streisand, everybody!

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:07.406
"Release Me" --
"Release Me 2" is out now.

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.509
Barbra, there's a rumor that
I wanted to ask you about

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.378
because we've talked about this
when you've been on the show

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:17.616
for years, and you said, "Oh, I
might be working on a memoir."

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:20.319
And everyone clapped and they
go, "Oh, that's amazing."

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.589
Then you came on
like two years later.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:26.225
We talked, and you go, "And then
I'm also working on a memoir,"

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.394
and everyone clapped.
-Right.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:31.364
-Were you lying to me or are you
working on this memoir?

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.798
-No, no, no, no.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:36.569
Actually, I started writing
things down in longhand

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:41.407
in my journals, you know,
like these kinds of things.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:45.144
I have like 20 of them,
which helped me write the book,

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.213
but I was always busy
doing something else,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.748
so I would write in the journals

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.382
and then go on
to something else.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:55.654
Actually, in 1984,
Jackie Kennedy came to me

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:59.225
and said, "I'd love to be
the editor of your book

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.660
at Doubleday," and we had tea.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.631
She was just so lovely
and she -- but I wasn't ready

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:10.636
to do that then, but I did
start writing in my journals,

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:15.408
and in 1999,
I really started writing,

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:19.379
and then other things and
concerts and movies or whatever.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:22.949
And then in 2008,
I really started writing.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.350
-Yes.
-What year is it now?

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.053
-Now it's 2021, Barbra.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:29.722
-2021.
-Yeah. What do you think?

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:33.926
-Fortunately, the pandemic
helped me finish the book.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:36.429
I'm almost finished.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:40.200
-No. This is what happened
last time!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.002
Almost finished? How almost?

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:47.440
-No, I've written 824 pages.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.210
And I still have
the little epilogue to do.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.313
And, you know, interesting --
my favorite number,

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:57.616
because I was born on the 24th,
is 24.

00:01:57.616 --> 00:02:01.888
This book is now 824 pages.
-Wow.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:08.862
-And it's 411,811,
something like that,

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:12.799
which if you add the numbers
together, they come up to 24.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.000
-Wow.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.602
-So it must be the right time
to release it.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.036
-Alright, so it's -- Wow.

00:02:18.036 --> 00:02:21.007
Alright, so that's basically
saying it's coming out.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.709
-It's coming out --
Yeah, next year.

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:24.810
-Okay.
-Soon.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.380
-How about a Barbra Streisand
biopic?

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.215
Would you be interested in that?

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.851
-No! No, no, no, no.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.586
That's for when you're gone.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.688
Somebody wants to play you.
I don't know.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.990
I don't want to see that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.960
I'm alive. I'm alive.
I'm still here.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.895
-I know, but everyone is
doing it now.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.731
It's kind of a thing.
People are doing it.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:47.900
-So I won't do it now.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:48.968
-Alright, perfect. Yeah.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.804
-Everybody else is doing it,
not me.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.473
-How about, like, a documentary
about you?

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:57.277
-Yes, you know, I've been
working on a documentary.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:03:00.113
I mean, over the years
we have at least --

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.315
Oh, we have about six hours
already,

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:05.384
but I haven't had time
to finish it.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.786
-Yeah, I understand.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:08.021
-I don't watch my movies

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.122
and I don't watch
my television specials

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.091
and I don't listen to
my records.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:14.761
-You should do all of them
because they're all fantastic.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:18.498
You really are amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.999
I love you.

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.601
The album is out now,
"Release Me 2."

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.406
Barbra, I hope to get to see you
in person next time, please.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.574
-Thank you.
Thank you for showing me that.

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:29.576
-I love you, buddy.

